{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"head -25 src/cljc/yang/{php,python,typescript}/antlr/{prelude,safepoint}.cljc; rg -n 'defn- missing|\\\\(missing ' src/cljc/yang/{php,python}/antlr/siteset.cljc; rg -n 'defn app\\\\*' src/cljc/yang/core/lower.cljc; find test -iname '*siteset*' -o -iname '*prelude*' -o -iname '*safepoint*' -o -iname '*lower*' | rg 'yang/(php|python|typescript)'\"","aggregated_output":"==> src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc <==\n(ns ^{:clj-kondo/config '{:lint-as {yang.php.antlr.quoted/defquoted clojure.core/def}}}\n yang.php.antlr.prelude\n  \"The PHP runtime profile, written as Universal AST\n   (docs/design/yang.php.md sections 3.5, 7, 9). PHP semantics for operators,\n   juggling, comparison, output and errors live here as guest code, not in\n   Clojure: the lowering only emits applications of these names.\n\n   Value encoding (P1):\n     int             host integer in [-2^63, 2^63-1] (a BigInt carrier on JS\n                     past 2^53); every operator computes the exact result\n                     through the `integer` module and demotes to float when\n                     it leaves the range\n     float           untagged Jing float64 content (`data/float64`), the\n                     shared ruling of yang.typescript.md section 2; the kind\n                     test is `php/kind`, never a second tag. The prelude\n                     holds no integral float literal (JS reads 1.0 as 1):\n                     floats are built with `data/float64` or computed, and\n                     host arithmetic only ever sees `data/float-value`\n     string          a host string whose every char is one byte (a latin-1\n                     carrier); the lowering resolves literal text to bytes\n     bool            host true / false\n     null            :php/null\n     array           {:php/type :array :index {key value} :order [key ...]\n                     :next-index n}: a persistent ordered map; keys are\n                     ints or strings (`php/array-key`); `:next-index` is\n\n==> src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/safepoint.cljc <==\n(ns yang.php.antlr.safepoint\n  \"The PHP `:loop` and `:call` hooks. A bounded run charges one safepoint to\n   its per-run counter; exhaustion unwinds past guest handlers and raises the\n   operational fatal, not a guest Throwable.\"\n  (:require\n    [yang.core.uast :as u]\n    [yang.core.module :as module]))\n\n\n(def profile\n  {:loop 'php.sp/loop, :call {:hook 'php.sp/call, :sequence true}})\n\n\n(def ticks-profile\n  \"Statement completion hooks for PHP's lexical ticks directives. This is\n   separate from the execution-budget profile so ticks do not charge it.\"\n  {:line {:hook 'php.sp/line, :operands true, :after true}})\n\n\n(def fatal-text\n  \"Maximum execution time of 30 seconds exceeded\")\n\n\n(def ^:private function-definitions\n  '[[php.sp/exhaust!\n\n==> src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/prelude.cljc <==\n(ns ^{:clj-kondo/config '{:lint-as {yang.python.antlr.prelude/defquoted clojure.core/def}}}\n yang.python.antlr.prelude\n  \"The Python runtime profile, written as Universal AST\n   (docs/design/yang.antlr.md §8.1, §8.2, §9.3). Python semantics for\n   operators, truthiness, equality, objects, exceptions and escapes live\n   here as guest code, not in Clojure: the lowering only emits applications\n   of these names.\n\n   Value encoding:\n     int             host integer (untagged)\n     float           {:py/float x}: tagged on every host, because JS cannot\n                     tell 2 from 2.0 (owner decision 3); x is float64\n                     content (`data/float64`), never a bare host number,\n                     so 2.0 has one address on every host. Arithmetic\n                     unwraps with `data/float-value` and computes on bare\n                     host numbers. The prelude holds no integral float\n                     literal (JS reads 1.0 as 1), and no float literal\n                     reaches host arithmetic except through\n                     `data/float-value`, which also bridges a float64\n                     carrier decoded from a row back to a host number:\n                     1.0 is written (data/float-value 1)\n     bool            host true / false (numeric as 1 / 0)\n     None            :py/None\n     str             {:py/str \\\"...\\\"}\n     list            a cell holding {:py/type :list :items [...]}\n\n==> src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/safepoint.cljc <==\n(ns yang.python.antlr.safepoint\n  \"The Python hook prelude for `yang.safepoint` (Architect safepoint\n   design, slice 1: signals; slice 2: recursion). Universal AST, like the\n   base prelude; the stage only places `(py.sp/loop)`, `(py.sp/call)` and\n   `(py.sp/return body)`, and what they mean is written here.\n\n   Signals. The composition hands the task a signal stream, a sealed\n   reference in the store under `signals-key`; a host adapter appends one\n   plain value per delivered signal. Each hook reads it with `stream/poll!`,\n   which answers `:dao.stream/blocked` rather than parking, so a program\n   with no signal pending never waits at a safepoint. On a signal (or a\n   gap: values were lost, so at least one arrived) the registered Python\n   handler is called with the signal and None, as CPython calls\n   `handler(signum, frame)`; with none registered, `KeyboardInterrupt` is\n   raised there, through `py/raise`: an explicit continuation invoke at an\n   explicit program point. Delivery is not journalled (owner decision 8).\n\n   Recursion (slice 2). Depth measures the current continuation: it is\n   `:base` plus `:depth` of the base prelude's dynamic-context record\n   `py.rt/ctx`, the one cell that also holds the handler stack (`:base` is\n   0 outside generators; each crossing into a generator sets it to the\n   resumer's absolute depth plus one). `py.sp/call`, at the head of every\n   Python function body, increments `:depth` and raises `RecursionError`\n   through `py/raise` when the absolute depth would exceed the limit;\n   `py.sp/return`, which the stage applies to the body's value, decrements\n\n==> src/cljc/yang/typescript/antlr/prelude.cljc <==\n(ns ^{:clj-kondo/config '{:lint-as {yang.typescript.antlr.prelude/defquoted clojure.core/def}}}\n yang.typescript.antlr.prelude\n  \"The `js` runtime profile, written as Universal AST\n   (docs/design/yang.typescript.md sections 3, 9, 10; the T1 plan's\n   section 6). JavaScript semantics for operators, coercion, equality,\n   strings, objects, functions and exceptions live here as guest code,\n   not in Clojure: the lowering only emits applications of these names.\n\n   Value encoding:\n     undefined, null  :js/undefined, :js/null (and the never guest-visible\n                      :js/tdz of an uninitialized binding): never host nil\n     boolean          host true / false\n     number           float64 content (`data/float64`) at the producer, on\n                      every host (JS cannot tell 2 from 2.0 as a bare\n                      Number). Arithmetic unwraps with `data/float-value`,\n                      computes on bare host doubles and rewraps with\n                      `data/float64`. The prelude holds no integral float\n                      literal: 1 is written (data/float64 1)\n     bigint           the bare exact integer, through `integer/*`; a number\n                      and a bigint are told apart by content equality with\n                      the same value as float64 (`js/kind-of`)\n     string           {:js/str s} when the code units are well-formed\n                      UTF-16, {:js/units [u ...]} otherwise; `js/mk-str` is\n                      the one normalizing door, so strict equality of\n                      strings is host `=`\n\n==> src/cljc/yang/typescript/antlr/safepoint.cljc <==\n(ns yang.typescript.antlr.safepoint\n  \"The `jssp` safepoint hook prelude (docs/design/yang.typescript.md\n   section 13; T1 plan section 8): `js.sp/loop` and `js.sp/call` for the\n   bundled profile and the linked `jssp` module. Universal AST, like the\n   base prelude; the `yang.safepoint` stage only places `(js.sp/loop)` and\n   `(js.sp/call)` at the `:loop` and `:call` sites the lowering marks, and\n   what they mean is written here.\n\n   Signals. The composition hands the task a signal stream, a sealed\n   reference in the store under `signals-key`; a host adapter appends one\n   plain value per delivered signal. Each hook reads it with `stream/poll!`,\n   which answers `:dao.stream/blocked` rather than parking, so a program\n   with no signal pending never waits at a safepoint. On a signal (or a\n   gap: values were lost, so at least one arrived) the hook delivers an\n   interrupt: it unwinds the handler stack to its outermost frame, the one\n   `js/run-main` installs, running every `finally` thunk on the way, and\n   throws the guest value `js.sp/interrupt` builds (an Error object named\n   `Interrupt`) through `js/throw` from there. No guest `catch` frame is\n   left to see it, so a `try`/`catch` around the loop does not catch it;\n   the run ends with it uncaught. Delivery is not journalled.\n\n   There is no depth accounting in T1: JavaScript has no RecursionError by\n   default (section 13), so `js.sp/call` is a poll only, and there is no\n   `:return` hook.\n\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/siteset.cljc:125:(defn- missing\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/siteset.cljc:248:      (absent? m) (missing manifest)\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/siteset.cljc:249:      (absent? r) (missing record-address)\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/siteset.cljc:250:      (absent? set) (missing set-address)\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/siteset.cljc:325:            (absent? body) (missing id)\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/siteset.cljc:161:(defn- missing\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/siteset.cljc:181:            (absent? body) (missing id)\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/siteset.cljc:239:      (absent? m) (missing manifest)\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/siteset.cljc:250:              (absent? record) (missing a)\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/siteset.cljc:251:              (absent? sites) (missing set-address)\n85:(defn app*\ntest/yang/php/antlr/safepoint_test.clj\ntest/yang/php/antlr/siteset_test.clj\ntest/yang/php/antlr/prelude_test.cljc\ntest/yang/php/antlr/lower_portable_test.cljc\ntest/yang/typescript/antlr/lower_test.clj\ntest/yang/typescript/antlr/safepoint_test.clj\ntest/yang/typescript/antlr/prelude_module_test.cljc\ntest/yang/typescript/antlr/class_prelude_test.cljc\ntest/yang/typescript/antlr/prelude_test.cljc\ntest/yang/typescript/antlr/lower_portable_test.cljc\ntest/yang/typescript/antlr/prelude_parity_test.cljc\ntest/yang/typescript/antlr/linked_prelude_test.cljc\ntest/yang/python/antlr/lower_test.clj\ntest/yang/python/antlr/linked_safepoint_test.cljc\ntest/yang/python/antlr/safepoint_programs.cljc\ntest/yang/python/antlr/siteset_test.cljc\ntest/yang/python/antlr/lower_portable_test.cljc\ntest/yang/python/antlr/safepoint_test.cljc\ntest/yang/python/antlr/prelude_parity_test.cljc\ntest/yang/python/antlr/linked_prelude_test.cljc\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
